This paper outlines the reasoning behind the validation of a reliable automotive driving system using the SSREF formal model. It explores the limitations of traditional safety-critical systems and introduces fail-functional concepts. The SSREF model is utilized to develop a fail-functional driving system, which is then evaluated through formal verification. The results of this analysis are discussed, revealing that a fail-functional approach for such critical systems may not be feasible. The discussion also touches on potential solutions, including alternative remedies for addressing potential system failures. The text is structured to conform to the ACM guidelines. The final section presents a conclusion. 

